# Behavioral Specification for `kmac_edn_timeout_error_vseq`

## 1. Scope

This specification describes the required behavior of the KMAC EDN timeout error verification sequence. The sequence exercises a KMAC operation in which entropy from the EDN is delayed until after the configured entropy wait-timer expires, causing the KMAC to report a wait-timer-expired error.

The sequence is a verification sequence rather than a synthesizable RTL block. Its externally observable behavior consists of KMAC configuration, stimulus, and checking actions performed in the verification environment.

## 2. Functional Behavior

- The sequence shall run between 1 and 20 KMAC operations per invocation.
- The sequence shall select an expected outcome using a weighted random distribution:
  - wait-timer-expired error, with 9/10 weight;
  - no error, with 1/10 weight.
- When wait-timer-expired is selected, the sequence shall:
  - configure the entropy wait timer so that expiration occurs before the delayed EDN response arrives;
  - disable the fast-entropy processing path;
  - not allow the environment to suppress generation of this error.
- When no error is selected, the sequence shall follow the normal operation path and shall not be required to produce the wait-timer-expired error.
- The selected outcome shall be fixed before the main operation begins.

## 3. Error Reporting Checks

For every operation that is expected to produce a wait-timer-expired error, the sequence shall verify:

- the KMAC error interrupt is asserted;
- the KMAC error code register reports a valid wait-timer-expired error;
- the error code information field is zero;
- the error is cleared after the error code has been checked;
- the KMAC operation completes and does not hang while waiting for entropy.

The sequence shall also ensure that the verified error code is read after the normal KMAC error-checking flow has completed.

## 4. KeyMgr Application Response Check

The sequence shall monitor the KeyMgr application response while the automated end-to-end data checking is disabled and before the entropy fetch for the current operation has completed.

The monitoring shall run concurrently with the rest of the sequence and shall not block the main operation flow.

When the KeyMgr response indicates that an operation has completed:

- if masking is enabled and the entropy mode is EDN, the sequence shall verify that the KeyMgr response also reports an error;
- if the expected error indication is absent, the sequence shall report a failure;
- the sequence shall wait for the completion indication to be deasserted before checking the next completion event.

This response check is required only when the above conditions are met. If masking is disabled, or if the operation does not use EDN entropy, no KeyMgr response error check is required.

## 5. Environment Behavior

- If masking is enabled, the sequence shall disable EDN testbench interface handshake assertions that are incompatible with an EDN request that is left pending until timeout.
- The sequence shall disable automated end-to-end data checking before starting.
- Automated end-to-end data checking shall remain disabled after the sequence finishes.
- The sequence shall not hang; if the KMAC operation does not reach a completed state after timeout, the sequence shall report a timeout failure.

## 6. Summary of Required Observable Outcomes

When this sequence completes successfully:

- the KMAC wait-timer-expired error path has been exercised;
- the KMAC error interrupt and error code have been validated;
- the KMAC operation has completed without deadlock;
- the KeyMgr application response error status has been checked when required;
- the sequence has left the environment in the expected disabled-scoreboard state.
